cff-version: 1.2.0
title: "HEAVEN: Autonomous Penetration-Testing Framework"
message: "If you use HEAVEN in your research, writeups, or tooling, please cite it using the metadata below."
type: software
authors:
  - given-names: Nisarg
    family-names: Chasmawala
    alias: HEAVEN
repository-code: "https://github.com/nishu2402/HEAVEN-Autonomous-Penetration-Testing"
url: "https://github.com/nishu2402/HEAVEN-Autonomous-Penetration-Testing"
abstract: >-
  HEAVEN is an autonomous offensive-security platform that
  automates reconnaissance, vulnerability detection, verified exploitation,
  risk triage, and reporting across web, network, Active Directory, and cloud
  targets. It pairs real detectors with an observe-plan-act LLM loop (with a
  deterministic fallback that needs no API key) and a hybrid machine-learning
  CVSS predictor, and runs from a CLI, a React web UI, and a REST plus
  WebSocket API.
